## 4. "Household hash" logic

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Households.java` — package-private helper computing the household id and member count. Full source:
```java
static String householdId(String lastName, String postcode) {
    if (postcode == null || postcode.isBlank()) { return null; }
    return Sha256.hex(normalizeName(lastName) + '|' + postcode).substring(0, 12);
}
static int memberCount(OwnerRepository repository, String householdId) {
    if (householdId == null) { return 0; }
    int count = 0;
    for (Owner owner : repository.findAll()) {
        if (householdId.equals(owner.getHouseholdId())) { count++; }
    }
    return count;
}
private static String normalizeName(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.strip().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```
Household id = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode`; null when no postcode.

Consumers:
- `AssignHousehold.java` — stamps `owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(lastName, postcode))`.
- `AssignHouseholdSize.java` — `owner.setHouseholdSize(Households.memberCount(...) + 1)`.
- `EnsureUniqueIdentity.java` — hard 409 if the household id is already occupied (bypassed by `sharesHousehold=true`; no postcode ⇒ no key ⇒ no collision).
